{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_cgrid_div_x",
    "description": "The zonal C-grid flux-form divergence rewrite target D(uh, wrt: x) on the mom6_cgrid: lowers the spatial derivative of the east-face layer volume flux field uh [i,j,k] to the cell divergence div_x(i,j,k) = (uh(i,j,k) - uh(i-1,j,k)) * IareaT(i,j) (the MOM6 continuity convergence (uh(i,j) - uh(i-1,j))*IareaT of continuity_zonal_convergence, MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:1085-1094, with uh the east-face flux of each cell and uh(i-1,j) the east-face flux of the west neighbor, i.e. the west face of cell (i,j)). SOLID-WALL BOUNDARIES: the west edge of cell i = 1 is a wall whose face flux is identically zero, so the i = 1 region is the EXPLICIT wall divergence div_x(1,j,k) = uh(1,j,k) * IareaT(1,j) — NOT the clamped difference (uh(1) - uh(1))*IareaT = 0 of a naive halo closure (the bug it replaces: a clamped west boundary silently zeroes the divergence of the first cell column). The east wall is carried by the flux rule, which emits the zero face flux at the east domain edge (i = N_I), so the interior region formula extends to i = N_I unchanged: div_x(N_I,j,k) = (0 - uh(N_I-1,j,k))*IareaT(N_I,j). The rule matches any D(uh, x) whose operand is a declared [i,j,k] field (esm-spec 9.6.1); IareaT is a free name resolved in the consuming model (the free-name contract of grids/mom6_cgrid/grid.esm). Pure telescoping difference of the face fluxes; the PPM reconstruction lives in the sibling mom6_cgrid_flux_x rule.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:mom6_cgrid",
      "grid:mom6_cgrid",
      "op:div",
      "order:1",
      "bc:wall",
      "axes:i,j,k",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "mom6_cgrid_div_x": {
      "params": ["uh"],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": ["uh"],
        "wrt": "x"
      },
      "where": {
        "uh": {
          "shape": ["i", "j", "k"]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [
            [2, "N_I"],
            [1, "N_J"],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ],
          [
            [1, 1],
            [1, "N_J"],
            [1, "N_K"]
          ]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j", "k"],
            "args": ["uh", "IareaT"],
            "ranges": {
              "i": [2, "N_I"],
              "j": [1, "N_J"],
              "k": [1, "N_K"]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["IareaT", "i", "j"]
                },
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["uh", "i", "j", "k"]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": ["uh", { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 1] }, "j", "k"]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": ["i", "j", "k"],
            "args": ["uh", "IareaT"],
            "ranges": {
              "i": [1, 1],
              "j": [1, "N_J"],
              "k": [1, "N_K"]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["IareaT", "i", "j"]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": ["uh", "i", "j", "k"]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
